In the release version of ggplot2 I hacked up my own log scale with breaks that suited my purposes.
How would I go about this with the new scales package (no ScaleLog10 in the new ggplot).

ScaleLogtime <- proto(ScaleLog10, funEnvir = globalenv(), {
    objname = "logtime"
    desc = "Position scale, time in seconds log10 transformed"
    doc=FALSE
    examples=function(.) {}

    ## Calculate our own breaks and labels and hand them off to ScaleLog10.
    ## It might be better to override the ScaleContinuous functions because
    ## when then data range is known, so could chose breaks based on that.
    new <- function(., ...)
    {
        ##print(c("ScaleLogtime$new",.,...))
        minors <- c(1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8,9)
        majors <- c(1,2,5)
        breaks <- c(c(1,5)*0.01, majors*0.1, majors*1, c(10,30),
                    majors*60, c(10,20)*60, majors*3600, majors*3600*10)
        minor_breaks <- c(minors*0.01, minors*0.1, minors, c(1,2,3,4,5)*10,
                          minors*60, minors*600, minors*3600, minors*3600*10)
        labels <- lapply(breaks,function(t) {
            if (t < 0.1)
                paste(formatC(t*1000,format="fg"),"ms",sep="")
            else if (t < 60)
                paste(formatC(t,format="fg"),"s",sep="")
            else if (t < 3600)
                paste(formatC(t/60,format="fg"),"m",sep="")
            else
                paste(formatC(t/3600,format="fg"),"h",sep="")
        })
        .super$new(.,breaks=breaks,labels=labels,minor_breaks=minor_breaks,...)
    }
})

Hi,

I am trying to reduce the number of legend values shown in the legend.
 I am working with the mpg dataset, and I have created a "honda"
subset of this data.  In this subset only a few "trans" values are
used, but when the plot is created all the potential "trans" values
are shown rather than only the values that are actually plotted.  Is
there a way to filter the labels so that they are not shown in the
legend.  Below is the code that I used to produce my current output.
Thanks for any help in advance,

-- Adam

<code>

library(ggplot2)

isa_match <- function(data_field, allowed_datum)
{
    for (d in allowed_datum){
        if (data_field == d){
           return (TRUE)
        }
    }
    return (FALSE)
}

subset_by_manu <- function(mpg_data, mpg_brand_filter){
    my_mpg_data <- data.frame(mpg_data[0,])
    for (i in 1:nrow(mpg_data)){
       if (isa_match(mpg_data[i,"manufacturer" ], mpg_brand_filter)){
           my_mpg_data <- rbind(my_mpg_data, data.frame(mpg_data[i,]))
       }
    }
    return (my_mpg_data)
}

honda <- subset_by_manu(mpg, c('honda'))

honda_plot <- ggplot()
honda_point <- geom_point( data=honda, mapping = aes(x = cty, y = hwy,
geom="jitter", size=displ, color=trans),  )
honda_facet <- facet_grid(fl ~ year)
honda_scale_size <- scale_size( to=c(3,4))

plot <- honda_plot + honda_point + honda_facet + honda_scale_size
print (plot)

